      "explanationAfterStep": "Hydride adds to the iminium carbon and makes the sixth and last stereocentre, where rings C and D meet. It arrives from the less hindered face and gives the more stable arrangement, in which the ring junction hydrogen is on the opposite face to the one in natural reserpine: Woodward obtained methyl O-acetylisoreserpate, epimeric with the natural series at this carbon. The app does not check stereochemistry yet."
