  "mechanismSummary": "Sodium borohydride delivers a hydride to the carbon of the dihydro-β-carbolinium ion, as in a reductive amination: two arrows, one step. The reduction makes the last stereocentre of the skeleton, at the carbon between the indole and the ring nitrogen, but the hydride arrives from the open face and gives the thermodynamically preferred arrangement: the iso series, epimeric with natural reserpine at that carbon. Woodward then corrected it by an epimerisation (see the concept card). The iminium counter-ion is drawn as chloride; the E-ring groups are drawn as labels; stereochemistry is explained, not yet checked.",
